  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1136 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nPresent model agreement continues to see the full exit of the\nweekend system with a ridge looking to build in behind it.\nHowever, cooler temperatures will look hold bring in some chilly\nmorning lows pushing most locations near freezing alongside some\nhints at widespread fog. Moving into the Tuesday and Wednesday\ndoes have present model agreement push another system across\nCentral Colorado. Currently, this position is not very favored for\nthe Panhandles with present ensemble giving the Panhandles a less\nthan 10 percent chance of precipitation. Still this passage has\ncontinue to trend towards some breezy to gusty conditions for the\nPanhandles with most models seeing the trough dip a portion of the\nPolar Jet over our north. By Thursday and end of next week,\npresent model runs do hint at another system that can bring more\nopportunities for precipitation. However, there is still a lot of\nuncertainty in these systems with current chances only around 10\nto 40 percent. Otherwise, temperatures are expected to warm\nslightly form the weekend activity but still stay in the 50 to 60s\nfor afternoon highs.",
